1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:11,650
In this video, we would like to introduce our project Smart Heating Control, which was created as part of the Smart Home Internship at the University of Media.

2
00:00:12,450 --> 00:00:18,650
In many offices, the heating is regulated manually, which is often inefficient and cumbersome.

3
00:00:19,250 --> 00:00:24,850
Our project aims to automate and optimize this process.

4
00:00:24,850 --> 00:00:35,650
Our system is specifically designed for teams working in offices. The idea is simple.

5
00:00:35,650 --> 00:00:42,050
When employees come to the office, they enter their attendance times in the Nextcloud calendar.

6
00:00:42,050 --> 00:00:47,250
Based on these entries, the heating is automatically controlled.

7
00:00:47,250 --> 00:00:53,050
We have used various components for the implementation.

8
00:00:53,050 --> 00:01:03,530
A Fritz-Box router as a smart hub, the intelligent radiator controllers from Fritz

9
00:01:03,530 --> 00:01:13,170
DECT 301 and 302, the frontend and backend for the user interface and control logic,

10
00:01:13,170 --> 00:01:21,410
a Raspberry Pi as the central control unit, and the integration of the Nextcloud calendar for

11
00:01:21,410 --> 00:01:29,090
recording attendance times. Our development work was carried out in parallel for

12
00:01:29,090 --> 00:01:38,690
the frontend and backend. A major challenge was to address the Fritz-Box

13
00:01:38,690 --> 00:01:47,170
and integrate the thermostats into the system. In addition to the technical integration

14
00:01:47,170 --> 00:01:53,770
of the thermostats, accessibility was important to us. Therefore, we support accessible

15
00:01:53,770 --> 00:02:00,210
components for interaction with the keyboard and screen readers. Additionally, we offer

16
00:02:00,210 --> 00:02:11,210
advanced settings such as text size adjustment, line spacing, and a sepia color filter, so that all team members can use the application.

17
00:02:11,210 --> 00:02:18,290
The frontend provides an overview of the rooms and various settings.

18
00:02:30,290 --> 00:02:33,890
Administrators can manage the entire system.

19
00:02:33,890 --> 00:02:46,050
The heating control is done via the Nextcloud team calendar. Employees enter

20
00:02:46,050 --> 00:02:51,890
the days they will be in the office. The system regularly checks the entries

21
00:02:51,890 --> 00:03:00,130
in the calendar and plans the heating control with the appropriate lead time. If employees

22
00:03:00,130 --> 00:03:07,810
do not come to the office or want to change the personally set temperature, they can do so at any time via the dashboard.
